{"body":"Refs #331 (not Closes: the owner-run live test and the cron entry are still to do).\n\n## What\n\nAdds the superclaude issue-watch command group (check-config, init-state, once, reset, status) in src/superclaude/cli/issue_watch/ (nine modules) with two registration lines in src/superclaude/cli/main.py. One timed poll cycle finds issues that carry a trigger label and an approval label from a listed approver, re-checks them against GitHub, writes a durable pending record, and only then starts one Orca claim session (/sc:issue --claim N). It never writes to GitHub, requests no issue text, and runs every process through one runner with no shell. Design: docs/designs/issue-watcher.md. Owner runbook: docs/designs/issue-watcher-setup.md.\n\n## Verification (all local, nothing live)\n\n- tests/issue_watch: 2637 passed, 0 skipped; same under xdist; also run on a real Python 3.10.20.\n- Wider affected set: 2667 passed, 1 pre-existing skip (tests/swarm/test_cli_registration.py:127, not touched).\n- make lint, pinned ruff 0.15.20 (check and format), make verify-sync, detect-secrets hook: clean. pyproject.toml, Makefile and .github are unchanged.\n- QA gates, each with 6 to 7 independent review agents, a single fix agent and two verifiers: Gate A (2 fix cycles), B (1), C (2), D (1), Final (1), M4 source-fidelity (1).\n\n## Post-execution reflect\n\nThe deep POST reflect returned FAIL (needs_human_decision) with one low-severity blocking regression, R-1: a launch could start up to one local save after the 120 s cut-off. The owner coordinator approved fixing it with a mutant-tested change and no repeat reflect (second commit). The new test fails against the pre-fix code and passes after. R-1 is fixed but NOT re-verified by a reflect. Accepted notes: R-2 and R-3 (new closed reasons cycle_complete and cycle_crashed, so 59 reason names against 57 in the design and spec; to be fixed at design), R-4 (record imports valid_operation_id), R-5 (five skip sites that are root or platform guards), R-6, R-7, and drift D-2 to D-4. Report: .dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-RF-issue-watcher-20261107-150955/reflect/post/REPORT.md.\n\n## Not verified here\n\n- The full test suite runs in CI only. A local run by one reviewer showed 4 failures outside issue_watch (a missing ruff module in the tool environment, a shared /tmp collision, an xdist thread-id check); CI will confirm.\n- gh and Orca reply shapes are assumed (fixtures under tests/issue_watch/fixtures/_assumed_shape/); several Orca behaviours are owner checks in the runbook.\n- Nothing was deployed, scheduled or run live; the watcher ships with enabled false.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","files":[{"path":".dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-RESEARCH-issue-watcher-20261107-064950/BUILD-REQUEST.md","additions":77,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-RESEARCH-issue-watcher-20261107-064950/RESEARCH-REPORT-issue-watcher.md","additions":2180,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-RESEARCH-issue-watcher-20261107-064950/TASK-RESEARCH-issue-watcher-20261107-064950.md","additions":528,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-RESEARCH-issue-watcher-20261107-064950/gaps-and-questions.md","additions":42,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-RESEARCH-issue-watcher-20261107-064950/phase-outputs/discovery/web-brief-what-we-know.md","additions":17,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-RESEARCH-issue-watcher-20261107-064950/phase-outputs/plans/gate3-verdict.md","additions":12,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-RESEARCH-issue-watcher-20261107-064950/phase-outputs/plans/gate4-verdict.md","additions":9,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-RESEARCH-issue-watcher-20261107-064950/phase-outputs/plans/phase3-gate-verdict.md","additions":8,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-R